## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design production-ready, on-device face verification systems with robust anti-spoofing capabilities under strict computational constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Edge-optimized inference architectures
- 3D head pose estimation from facial landmarks
- Temporal liveness detection for spoof resistance
- Parameter-efficient 5-shot adaptation via adapter layers
- Hybrid synthetic-to-real data generation strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: unified inference pipeline
function processFrame(frame) {
  const backbone = extractFeatures(frame);
  const detection = faceDetectionHead(backbone);
  const liveness = temporalLivenessHead(backbone);
  return { detection, liveness };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This assesses end-to-end CV system design on monocular input, 3D reconstruction, semantic/kinematic outputs, and on-device adaptation, under real-world constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth/3D reconstruction
- Voxel-based 3D representation and BEV outputs
- Multi-task objectives: occupancy, semantics, motion tracking
- Self-supervision with ego-motion and photometric consistency
- Lightweight 3-shot on-device adaptation via adapters

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch
async function runPipeline(frame) {
  const latent = encode(frame)
  const voxels = decodeToVoxels(latent)
  return { occupancy: voxelToOccupancy(voxels), beings: trackPedestrians(latent) }
}
```

